  ## Key Changes

  - Rename study UI copy from “goal” to “quest” / “target concept.”
  - Replace goalCandidates(detail) behavior with quest-target helpers:
      - Recommended quests = milestone nodes.
      - Milestone node = non-foundational target with trusted prerequisite ancestors and no trusted outgoing dependent edges.
      - If fewer than 3 milestones exist, fill from highest journeySize > 0.
      - Cap recommended quests at 8.
      - Search still exposes all concepts as advanced target concepts.

  - Keep route/API shape unchanged: target=<derivedNodeId> remains the technical target.
  - Add quest graph scoping:
      - questCone = trusted prerequisite ancestors + target.
      - If cone size is <= 9, show the full quest cone.
      - If cone size is > 9, show the current frontier neighborhood intersected with the quest cone, always including the target.
      - Add a “Quest / Full map” toggle; Full map preserves today’s whole-layer graph.

  - Preserve existing learner-state behavior:
      - Mastered/frontier/locked classification still comes from composeStudySession.
      - Known-closure hiding still applies in adapted quest view.
      - “Goal reached” becomes “Quest complete.”

  ## Implementation Notes

  - Keep reusable pure graph helpers near the existing derived graph helpers first, then promote to @lrnki/application only if the
    Learner App starts consuming them.

  - Update GoalPicker into a quest picker with “Recommended quests” and “Search all target concepts.”
  - Update StudySession to compute visible quest detail before passing it to DerivedGraphExplorer.
  - Add minimal optional copy props to DerivedGraphExplorer if needed so the card can say “Quest map” without changing the neutral
    enrichment page.

  - Update CONTEXT.md with Study Target as the technical term if implementation renames public domain language; add an Auto Quest
    Chain TODO, not an ADR.

  ## Test Plan

  - Unit-test milestone selection, fallback fill, search-all behavior, and sorting.
  - Unit-test quest cone and 9-node cap behavior.
  - Unit-test large-cone visible set: frontier neighborhood intersected with cone plus target.
  - Regression-test current Rust graph expectation: recommended quests should include terminal milestones like Move semantics, String
    Type, Copy trait, Memory management, and Variable Scope, not every foundational node.

  - Run admin-lab tests and typecheck.
  - Real-use gate: inspect /admin/lab/study on the latest Rust enrichment and one non-Rust enrichment to confirm the page feels like
    focused quests, not a full graph picker.

  ## Assumptions

  - Auto Quest Chain is deferred; Quest Subgraph is the simpler intermediate step.
  - 9 is the visible full-cone cap.
  - Whole graph remains available as context, but not as the default active learning goal.
